      "level": 1,
      "topic": "business & finance",
      "title_zh": "十二个小时的班",
      "title_en": "A twelve-hour shift",
      "paragraphs": [
        ["这些", "天", "工作", "很", "多", "。", "今天", "，", "我", "上", "了", "十二", "个", "小时", "的", "班", "。", "我", "都", "没", "时间", "吃", "东西", "。"],
        ["晚上", "回家", "，", "我", "非常", "累", "。", "我", "什么", "都", "不", "想", "做", "，", "就", "坐", "在", "床", "上", "。"],
        ["妈妈", "给", "我", "打", "了", "电话", "。", "她", "说", "：", "“", "钱", "很", "重要", "，", "身体", "最", "重要", "！", "你", "要", "多", "休息", "。", "”"],
        ["我", "说", "：", "“", "好", "，", "明天", "我", "早", "点", "回家", "。", "”"]
      ],
      "translations": [
        "There's been lots of work these days. Today I did a twelve-hour shift. I didn’t even have time to eat.",
        "When I got home in the evening I was exhausted. I didn't want to do anything, so I just sat on the bed.",
        "Mum phoned me. She said: “Money matters, but your health matters most! You need to rest more.”",
        "I said: “OK, I’ll come home early tomorrow.”"
      ],
      "names": [],
      "new_words": ["班", "累", "休息"],
      "glossary": [
        { "word": "班", "english": "shift (上班: to work a shift)" },
        { "word": "累", "english": "tired" },
        { "word": "休息", "english": "to rest" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2026-10-17-s2",
      "level": 1,
      "topic": "football",
      "title_zh": "一边吃一边看",
      "title_en": "Eating and watching",
      "paragraphs": [
        ["今天", "晚上", "有", "曼联", "的", "球", "。", "我", "和", "朋友", "们", "一边", "吃", "肉", "，", "一边", "看", "球", "。"],
        ["有的", "朋友", "喜欢", "曼联", "，", "有的", "不", "喜欢", "。"],
        ["曼联", "进", "球", "的", "时候", "，", "我", "马上", "站", "起来", "了", "，", "我", "的", "一", "个", "朋友", "没", "站", "起来", "。"],
        ["最后", "是", "二", "比", "一", "。", "我", "很", "高兴", "。", "那", "个", "朋友", "不", "太", "高兴", "，", "他", "不", "喜欢", "曼联", "。"],
        ["我", "说", "：", "“", "别", "不", "高兴", "，", "再", "吃", "点", "肉", "吧", "！", "”"]
      ],
      "translations": [
        "Man United were playing this evening. My friends and I ate meat while we watched.",
        "Some of my friends like Man United, and some don't.",
        "When Man United scored, I jumped straight up, but one of my friends stayed sitting down.",
        "In the end it was two–one. I was really happy. That friend wasn’t so happy — he doesn’t like Man United.",
        "I said: “Cheer up — have some more meat!”"
      ],
      "names": ["曼联"],
      "new_words": ["一边", "肉", "有的"],
      "glossary": [
        { "word": "一边", "english": "while (一边…一边…: doing two things at once)" },
        { "word": "肉", "english": "meat" },
        { "word": "有的", "english": "some" },
        { "word": "曼联", "english": "Manchester United" }
      ]
    }
  ],
